.TH ALACRITTYFORGE 1 "October 2026" "alacrittyForge v1.1.0" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
alacrittyforge \- Alacritty's settings, without editing the file by hand
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B alacrittyforge
.br
.B alacrittyforge \-\-version
.br
.B alacrittyforge \-\-help
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B alacrittyForge
is a keyboard-driven terminal application for the settings of the
.BR alacritty (1)
terminal. Every setting has a plain name and an explanation, known values
are picked from lists and presets, and every change is reviewed
(old \(-> new) and backed up before it is written.
.PP
A save touches only the settings that changed: comments and layout in
.I alacritty.toml
are kept. The new file is checked, written next to the old one and swapped
in, so it is never left half-written; a file that is a symbolic link stays
one. A file that cannot be read is never saved over.
.PP
Alacritty picks a saved change up by itself, in every open window, unless
.I general.live_config_reload
is off. alacrittyForge reads
.B alacritty \-\-version
and writes the setting names that version reads (Alacritty 0.14 moved
.IR import ,
.IR working_directory ,
.IR live_config_reload ,
.I ipc_socket
into
.I [general]
and
.I shell
into
.IR [terminal] ).
.PP
No root privileges are needed: alacrittyForge only changes the user's own
files.
.PP
The full manual is inside the application (press
.BR M ,
or
.B F1
on a setting for its page) and in
.I /usr/lib/alacrittyforge/alacrittyforge/manual/
as Markdown.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the usage and exit.
.
.SH SCREENS
.TP
.B 1 \- Overview
Your terminal at a glance; what needs attention (a file that cannot be
read, settings with old names, settings Alacritty does not know, no
monospace font), with the button that fixes it; safety; common tasks.
.TP
.B 2 \- Settings
Every Alacritty setting on Linux in eight groups: Window, Text, Cursor,
Scrolling & copy, Bell, Shell & start, Mouse & links, Advanced. A setting
the file does not set shows what Alacritty does instead.
.TP
.B 3 \- Themes
Theme files in
.I ~/.config/alacritty/themes
with a preview in their colours; use one, adjust its colours (saved as your
own copy), install one. Files another tool maintains are locked.
.TP
.B 4 \- Shortcuts
Your keyboard shortcuts and Alacritty's own, in words. Add one by pressing
its keys; turn off one of Alacritty's.
.TP
.B 5 \- Backups
Why each backup was made and what restoring it would change.
.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B Tab ", " Shift+Tab
Next / previous field or button.
.TP
.B Enter
Open a list, press a button, confirm.
.TP
.B Space
Flip a switch.
.TP
.B Up ", " Down
In a number: step through its presets.
.TP
.B Esc
Close a window.
.TP
.B 1 \(en 6 ", " Ctrl+letter
Go to a menu entry: the five screens, then Help (6, Ctrl+H). The letter is
the one underlined in the menu bar.
.TP
.B F10 ", " S
Save, with a review first.
.TP
.B R
Read the file again; unsaved changes stay.
.TP
.B F1
Help on what is selected.
.TP
.B M
The manual.
.TP
.B ?
All keys.
.TP
.B Q ", " Ctrl+Q
Quit; asks first if something is not saved.
.TP
.B Enter ", " A ", " I
Themes: use a theme, adjust its colours, install one.
.TP
.B + ", " F2 ", " Delete
Shortcuts: add, change, remove.
.TP
.B R ", " N ", " D
Backups: restore, back up now, delete.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/alacritty/alacritty.toml
Alacritty's settings. Read and written by alacrittyForge.
.TP
.I ~/.config/alacritty/themes/
Theme files.
.TP
.I ~/.config/alacritty/backups/
Backups (the newest 20), each with a note saying why it was made.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/alacrittyforge/logs/
One line per run, by day.
.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Linux with Alacritty 0.13 or newer; Python 3.11 or newer; python-textual,
python-rich, python-tomlkit and python-forgekit 0.10.0 or newer; fontconfig.
.
